.TH GOBAN-CLIENT 1 "August 2026" "goban" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
goban-client \- inspect and control a running goban-daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B goban-client
[\-\-sock \fIPATH\fR]
[\-\-json]
.I COMMAND
[\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B goban-client
uses the daemon's Unix socket to inspect health and effective rule settings,
list confirmed kernel bans, apply manual changes, request transactional reload,
and test a loaded rule through the production processing pipeline.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show version, uptime, source/rule counts, degraded-source count, dropped lines,
active bans, and any firewall-list error.
.TP
.B sources
Show each source's lifecycle status, subscriber count, delivered/dropped
records, reconnects, last event, and last error.
.TP
.B rules
Show effective rules and counters. JSON output includes regex, date policy,
allowlists, exclusions, trusted-proxy settings, and strike snapshots.
.TP
.B "list" | " banned"
List currently active kernel bans with rule attribution, TTL, and expiration
when available.
.TP
.B "ban " \fIIP\fR " \-\-rule " \fILABEL\fR " [\-\-ttl " \fIDURATION\fR "]"
Apply a manual confirmed ban. TTL defaults to one hour and must fit the same
kernel-safe limits as configured rules.
.TP
.B "unban " \fIIP\fR
Remove a ban. A successful operation is written to the audit stream.
.TP
.B reload
Strictly load and transactionally apply reloadable configuration. Candidate
validation/startup failure leaves the active graph running.
.TP
.B "test \-\-rule " \fINAME\fR " " \fILOGFILE\fR " | " \-
Fetch the complete effective rule and run it against a file or stdin using the
same matcher, 16-KiB record bound, timestamp policy, exclusions, global and
per-rule allowlists, trusted-proxy gate, and tracker. A noop banner prevents
kernel changes.
.TP
.B version
Print client version.
.SH GLOBAL FLAGS
.TP
.B \-\-sock " " \fIPATH\fR
Override the daemon socket (default /run/goban/goban.sock).
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit JSON for status, sources, rules, or banned.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
goban-client status
goban-client sources
goban-client --json rules | jq .
goban-client list
goban-client ban 198.51.100.7 --rule manual --ttl 12h
goban-client unban 198.51.100.7
goban-client test --rule sshd /var/log/auth.log.1
goban-client reload
.fi
.SH PERMISSIONS
The socket normally has mode 0660 and the configured group owner. Membership
permits manual bans, unbans, and reloads; grant it as an administrative
privilege.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Command succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
Socket, validation, or daemon operation failed.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR goban-daemon (8)
